<title>GERMANY: German metal sector pay talks end, resume Tuesday.</title>
<headline>German metal sector pay talks end, resume Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>SULZBACH, Germany 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pay talks between German engineering trade union IG Metall and metal sector employers were broken off on Monday evening and were to be resumed on Tuesday, union officials said.</p>
<p>Leaving the talks, IG Metall chairman Klaus Zwickel refused to comment on how negotiations with the employers's federation Gesamtmetall had gone so far, but said they would resume at 0900 GMT Tuesday.</p>
<p>The talks, expected to continue until Wednesday, concern the 1997 pay-round for the industry and planned cuts to a number of worker bonuses.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
